FFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]memory_config_section.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/memory_config_section.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ia[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ia/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Nested glossary scope diagnostic in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-scope[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-scope: teach the Rust config provenance pass to diagnose a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]non-local `memory.glossary` in addition to the legacy top-level [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`glossary`, and extend the config parity test to cover both paths.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Config schema, deprecation registry, and packaged defaults[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]config-surface[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-scope[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]config-surface: add the `memory` object with `h1_title` and `glossary` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to sase.schema.json, mark the two legacy top-level keys deprecated, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]register them in DEPRECATED_TOP_LEVEL_KEYS, restructure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default_config.yml, and update the schema and inventory tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Nested reads with legacy fallback[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]read-sites[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]read-sites: add one shared glossary-location resolver, read [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`memory.h1_title` and `memory.glossary` first with a legacy fallback in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the AMD title loader, the memory init glossary loader, and the editor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glossary catalog, and update every affected test fixture.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate sase's own config and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]self-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after config-surface, read-sites[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]self-migration: move this repository's own `sase/sase.yml` keys under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`memory:`, regenerate memory, and rewrite the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]configuration/init/memory/xprompt/ace docs to document the canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]paths and the deprecated aliases.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate downstream repository configs[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]downstream-repos[dim] · [dim][/dim]after config-surface, read-sites[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]downstream-repos: migrate the bob-cli project config and the chezmoi [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]user overlay to the nested form, correct the sase-nvim README reference,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and confirm actstat needs no change.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ia","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-ia.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e72d81607844276dbf45215d70e70baa","started_at":"2026-08-09T14:27:07.142568+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia","bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-ia.land"]}
